meta {
  name: 2 Get thread
  type: http
  seq: 2
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/messages/thread/{{providerEmail}}
  body: none
}
docs {
  One conversation, keyed on the **counterpart's email address** — not on `threadId`. The server sorts
  the caller's own claim together with this address to derive the thread, so with the caller always
  supplying one side a thread between two other people has no representation in this URL space at all:
  it is unrequestable rather than merely refused.

  Swap `{{providerEmail}}` for `{{customerEmail}}` when running this as the provider.

  Same flat `MessageEntity` array as the inbox. An empty array is `200` — it means nothing has been
  said yet, which is a valid state for a thread you are about to start.
}
